## Predeclared signals

### Gate-P direct-crossover PASS

Requires all of:

1. zero correctness failures;
2. exact P12/P13 final-decision invariance on all 332 frozen cases;
3. at least one Gate-P case dispatched to P6 and consuming a fold;
4. P13/direct source-inclusive case-balanced geomean <= `0.95`;
5. bootstrap 95% upper bound < `1.00`;
6. no greater than 5% pooled increase in pair terms or peak monomials versus direct.

### Deferred-pair engineering success

Independently report success if all hold:

1. exact P12/P13 final-decision invariance;
2. P13/P12 source-build+dispatch case-balanced geomean <= `0.95`;
3. P13/P12 source-inclusive case-balanced geomean <= `0.99`;
4. bootstrap 95% upper bound for P13/P12 source-inclusive < `1.00`.

## Guardrails

- No frozen tree value, cutoff, fold threshold, case, repetition count, endpoint, pair representation, or exactification order may change after P13 results are seen.
- No P13 timing may be used to modify the Stage-1 shortcut, Stage-2 counting routine, reuse-scan structure, or early-abort rule.
- No learned gate, case-specific exception, approximate duplicate filter, or post-hoc dispatch threshold is permitted.
- P13 is a CPython implementation experiment. A win would demonstrate cheaper exposure of the already-frozen folding/dispatch mechanism; it would not establish uniqueness to CM or general natural-circuit acceleration.
